{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Nature's Force", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Volcanoes", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 14, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "base", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the bottom part of an object", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Most people who live at the base of a volcano or have witnessed a volcanic eruption share the belief that volcanoes are one of the most fascinating phenomena in nature.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about volcanos.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "phenomena", "type": "name"}, {"content": "anything that is or can be experienced or felt", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Volcanoes are one of the most fascinating phenomena in nature. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "volcanologist", "type": "name"}, {"content": "geologist who studies the eruptive activity and formation of volcanoes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I gathered a lot of information which began the start of my career as a volcanologist.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "apparent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "able to be seen or understood", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I wouldn't have gone at all until it became apparent that I couldn't become a bona fide volcanologist without a degree.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bona fide", "type": "name"}, {"content": " authentic or genuine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I couldn't become a bona fide volcanologist without a degree.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "permanent", "type": "name"}, {"content": " lasting for a long time or forever", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If a volcano is active, it is in a state of permanent eruption.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cinders", "type": "name"}, {"content": "small pieces of partly burned coal or wood", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Volcanic material, which consists of heated rocks, ash and cinders, is projected with tremendous force.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to eject", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to forcefully and quickly send out", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This volcanic material can fall on the outside of the volcano or return to the inside of the volcano through the crater and be ejected again.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dormant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not presently active", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A volcano may be active for many years and then become dormant or inactive.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob05aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "inactive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "doing nothing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Inactive volcanoes are also monitored.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob05aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Speculating about Past Events: <span class=\"italic\">Would Have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Didn't Need To</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use <span class=\"strong\">would have</span> and <span class=\"strong\">didn't need to </span> to speculate about past events.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">would have </span> to express events that did not actually happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">would have </span>called you, but I didn't want to use up any more minutes on my cell.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use <span class=\"strong\">would have </span> to make assumptions about the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Someone left the door open? That <span class=\"strong\">would have</span> been James, most likely.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">didn't need to </span> to express an unnecessary action that was not actually done.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">My computer was a bit slow, but fortunately it <span class=\"strong\">didn't need to </span>be replaced.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Note: You can also use <span class=\"strong\">needn't</span> + <span class=\"strong\">have</span> to refer to an unnecessary action that was actually done, but this is mainly used in British English. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">needn't have</span> come all the way out here to visit me.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here are a few examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">didn't need to</span> be reminded of the great force of nature and the possible destruction that might ensue. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't have lived </span>by a volcano for such a long period of time, but we had such a keen fascination with them.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Relative Clauses: <span class=\"strong\">Who</span>, <span class=\"strong\">Whom</span> and <span class=\"strong\">Whose</span> ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " The relative pronouns <span class=\"strong\">who</span>, <span class=\"strong\">whom</span> and <span class=\"strong\">whose</span>  are used to provide information about the people introduced in your sentences.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">who </span> to refer to the subject of a sentence, if it is a person.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">He is the person <span class=\"strong\">who</span> cleans the floors.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Whom</span> is the object form of <span class=\"strong\">who.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">He is the person <span class=\"strong\">whom </span>I met at the conference last week.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Note: In colloquial speech, <span class=\"strong\">who </span> is commonly used in place of <span class=\"strong\">whom</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You also use <span class=\"strong\">whom</span> when it follows a preposition.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">To <span class=\"strong\">whom </span>should I send the payment?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Note: Again, in colloquial speech, <span class=\"strong\">who </span> is commonly used in place of <span class=\"strong\">whom. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Who </span>should I send the payment to?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">whose </span> when you are talking about possession.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">This is my friend <span class=\"strong\">whose </span>brother owns the bakery.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">My friend, <span class=\"strong\">whose </span>brother owns a bakery, is coming over.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here are a few examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Most people <span class=\"strong\">who</span> live at the base of a volcano have witnessed a volcanic eruption .", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My father, with <span class=\"strong\">whom</span> I shared the passion of geology , told me that one of the main classifications in volcanology is determining whether a volcano is active or inactive.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My father, <span class=\"strong\">whose</span> knowledge and experience was vast, told me that a volcano may be active for many years. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": " Go online and watch a video on volcano watchers on YouTube.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take notes on the main ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your notes with a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss what you think of the people in the video and what they do.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I watch a video about volcano watchers.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write down main ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I tell a friend what I saw, learned and wrote down.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss with my friend what I think about what the people in the video do.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about geography, climate and environmental problems.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can speculate about something in the past. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can report facts about events or actions using words like <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, <span class=\"italic\">whom</span> and <span class=\"italic\">whose</span>. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How much do you know about volcanoes?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What volcanoes have you heard about?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Tell me about volcanoes.", "type": "free_type_text_area"}],