g_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le14ob05re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Most people who live at the base of a volcano or have witnessed a volcanic eruption share the belief that volcanoes are one of the most fascinating phenomena in nature. It is to me.\n<br>\nWhen my family and I lived beneath the volcano as a child I wouldn't have been surprised if it had erupted. I didn't need to be reminded of the great force of nature and the possible destruction that might ensue. I gathered a lot of information which began the start of my career as a volcanologist. I hardly needed to go to university because of all that I learned on my own and all my father taught me. I wouldn't have gone at all until it became apparent that I couldn't become a bona fide volcanologist without a degree.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le14ob05re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Volcanologists learn about volcanoes through the field of geology, which is the study of the earth and its rocks.  My father,  with whom I shared the passion of geology, told me that one of the main classifications in volcanology is determining whether a volcano is active or inactive. If a volcano is active, it is in a state of permanent eruption.\n<br>\nVolcanic material, which consists of heated rocks, ash and cinders, is projected with tremendous force. This volcanic material can fall on the outside of the volcano or return to the inside of the volcano through the crater and be ejected again. Lava that flows over the rim of the crater is even hot enough to melt ice in a matter of seconds.", "id": 2, "time": "41000", "image": "engenn10le14ob05re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "My father, whose knowledge and experience was vast, told me that a volcano may be active for many years and then become dormant or inactive.\n<br>\nVolcanoes fascinate me and my father because they show the violent energy which is hidden under the earth. Although giant eruptions are not common, they remain proof there are forces under the earth that are beyond human control.\n<br>\nWe wouldn't have lived by a volcano for such a long period of time, but we had such a keen fascination with them. Nobody needed to tell us that we were taking an enormous risk by living there.", "id": 3, "time": "84300", "image": "engenn10le14ob05re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn10le14ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le14ob05re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}]}]}